Task 1 — `task_01.md` (product, #982 slice 1). Two shell commands print an error and still exit 0. yoyo model nosuch-model-x should exit 2 (usage error) and yoyo skill show <missing> should exit 1. The task reuses the existing shell_exit_code / exit_if_failed setup from 6d84deff. It requires before/after exit codes measured on the binary, and a check that any in-process dispatch test of these commands won't be killed when they start exiting. Whether find/def with no match should exit 1 is still an open decision and stays out of scope.

